_Package() is emitted only as a NATIVE function (codegen/emit_pkg_descriptor.bn + native/*/_pkg_descriptor.bn); in the bytecode VM only the four builtin packages reach their _Package, via the hardcoded externs in vm/extern_register_std.bn.  A user/stdlib package compiled to bytecode has no native _Package symbol, so the VM reports "extern not found: <pkg>._Package".  Fixing it (a major VM-backend project) means emitting _Package + its static-managed descriptor as bytecode per package so the VM runs it directly, replacing the hardcoded-builtin extern table.  (int-int additionally hits the pre-existing multi-package double-VM failure.)  Tracked in claude-todo.md.
